    <title>Disorder-Driven Localisation in Moire Systems</title>
    <summary>  Flat bands amplify interaction effects because the kinetic scale is quenched.
Existing simulations cannot reach the system sizes at which the localisation
length saturates. We perform large-scale exact diagonalisation on clusters of up
to $N = 24$ sites. The gap closes at a critical twist angle $\theta_c =
1.09^{\circ}$. This identifies a concrete experimental signature.
</summary>
    <author><name>S. Okonkwo</name></author>
